WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.770 --> 00:00:05.870
Sure your mobile phone will give you the
time, but not nearly as conveniently or

00:00:05.870 --> 00:00:07.940
fashionably as a wristwatch does.

00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:13.850
Watches come in a variety of materials,
often combined with stainless steel, but one

00:00:13.850 --> 00:00:17.150
of the more creative pairings is stainless
steel with wood.

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:24.710
This company makes wristwatches, which
feature exotic hardwood accents.

00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:31.100
This particular model is a limited edition
series designed for New York Yankees baseball

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:36.680
fans. The blue painted maple comes from
wooden seats salvaged from the original

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:39.650
Yankee Stadium, which opened in 1923.

00:00:42.310 --> 00:00:47.350
At the watch factory, a worker first cuts a
strip of wood just over a third of an inch

00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:52.030
thick, then cuts it into blocks, measuring
around three fourths of an inch by a third of

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:57.910
an inch each. Manufacturers will ultimately
use these blocks to make the wood inlays and

00:00:57.910 --> 00:00:59.590
the links of the watch bracelet.

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:04.300
The worker then cuts another strip from a
piece of wood, this one nearly a quarter of

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:09.350
an inch thick. The worker then cuts this
strip into nearly two by two inch squares.

00:01:09.370 --> 00:01:13.720
Each one will become a ring called a bezel
that goes around the watch dial.

00:01:14.170 --> 00:01:18.850
Another worker mounts one square at a time
on a lathe and bores a hole through the

00:01:18.850 --> 00:01:26.870
middle. She mounts several board squares
onto a steel mandrel that attaches to the

00:01:26.870 --> 00:01:29.270
lathe along with a bezel template.

00:01:29.810 --> 00:01:35.360
As the lathe turns a steel roughing gouge,
rounds the squares to the diameter of the

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:42.360
template. She takes one bezel at a time and
cuts it to the required thickness about a

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:43.470
10th of an inch.

00:01:44.190 --> 00:01:49.980
She then shaves wood from the underside so as
not to remove the historic blue paint on top.

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:54.910
To make the watch case which houses the dial
and movement.

00:01:54.940 --> 00:01:59.020
The manufacturers cut a blank piece of
extruded stainless steel.

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:03.060
Then place it in a computer guided machine.

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:09.190
Under a continuous shower of lubricant.

00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:14.260
The machine's 12 different tools take turns
shaping the piece into a watch case.

00:02:17.540 --> 00:02:23.120
The first tools bore a hole in the middle
for the movement and carve a groove around

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:24.740
the hole for the wood bezel.

00:02:25.550 --> 00:02:30.890
The next tools cut the outside profile of
the case and the lugs for attaching the watch

00:02:30.890 --> 00:02:36.800
band. Then the final tool drills holes in
the lugs for the spring loaded pins that

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:38.990
attach the watch band to the case.

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:46.210
Another computer guided machine makes the
watchband and links out of a bar of stainless

00:02:46.210 --> 00:02:51.930
steel. This machine reduces the bar in
width, carves out the links and bores holes

00:02:51.930 --> 00:02:53.430
for the connecting pins.

00:02:53.970 --> 00:02:55.150
A process called.

00:02:55.170 --> 00:02:59.190
Iron plating puts a black finish on all the
stainless steel parts.

00:02:59.790 --> 00:03:04.590
Then a worker assembles two bands and
connects one to the watch clasp.

00:03:05.310 --> 00:03:08.480
Next, he attaches the watch case window.

00:03:08.490 --> 00:03:13.350
It's made of sapphire glass, a crystal
that's exceptionally durable.

00:03:13.530 --> 00:03:15.840
He inserts the Self-winding movement in
dial.

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:22.200
The dial is a sheet of brass with cut out
numbers and indices over a base coated in

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:23.220
luminescent paint.

00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:25.140
The watch glows in the dark.

00:03:26.370 --> 00:03:32.130
He secures the movement to the case with the
retaining ring, then inserts the crown, which

00:03:32.130 --> 00:03:33.840
sets the dials hands.

00:03:34.230 --> 00:03:37.410
The worker screws on the stainless steel
case back.

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:42.240
The watch's window of sapphire glass allows
you to see the working movement inside.

00:03:42.810 --> 00:03:47.830
The Caseback is engraved with the name of
the limited edition collection, and this

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:49.630
watch is number in the series.

00:03:50.710 --> 00:03:54.370
He attaches the watchband to the case with
spring pins.

00:03:57.640 --> 00:04:02.920
With the watch now fully assembled, it's
time to inlay the Yankee Stadium wooden chair

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:06.950
accents. Using a toothpick.

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:11.450
A worker applies epoxy glue to the
rectangular recess in each link.

00:04:15.700 --> 00:04:17.950
Then he places a wooden link piece in each
recess.

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:34.180
He follows the same process for the dials.

00:04:34.180 --> 00:04:42.110
Wooden bezel. A worker sets the watch aside
for 24 hours to let the adhesive set.

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:49.130
Then the worker buffs the entire surface on
a cloth polishing wheel.

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:55.220
This process removes the fingerprints and
dust and smooths those historic wood accents.

00:04:55.280 --> 00:05:00.950
The watch automatically winds with wrist
movement to reliably tell the time while

00:05:00.950 --> 00:05:03.560
nostalgically going back in time.

00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:10.240
Before the invention of electricity,
criminal acts were hidden by darkness.

00:05:10.270 --> 00:05:14.680
Police officers carried special lanterns as
they pursued suspects.

00:05:14.710 --> 00:05:19.870
Today, craftsmen replicate these lanterns
for the movie and television industries.

00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:27.430
These props are authentically replicated
pieces of police history with a thick bull's

00:05:27.430 --> 00:05:29.560
eye lens to magnify the light from the
flame.

00:05:30.190 --> 00:05:35.260
The 19th century police lantern helped find
bad guys on shadowy streets.

00:05:37.540 --> 00:05:43.420
To replicate a vintage police lantern, the
craftsman starts with a piece of steel using

00:05:43.420 --> 00:05:48.430
a scribe. He traces around a pattern to
transfer the outline to the blank.

00:05:48.520 --> 00:05:53.860
He marks notches for hinges and for the
latch and etches the shape of the lens hole

00:05:53.860 --> 00:06:00.080
in the center. He draws two diagonal lines
in the lens hole area.

00:06:00.230 --> 00:06:04.370
The point where the lines intersect
determines the exact center.

00:06:05.270 --> 00:06:08.720
He punches a divot into the steel at this
cross point.

00:06:13.460 --> 00:06:17.960
He scribes lines along the edges for bending
into a reinforced border.

00:06:17.960 --> 00:06:22.250
Later on, he cuts out the hinge and latch
notches.

00:06:22.910 --> 00:06:25.520
Following the transferred pattern lines.

00:06:29.620 --> 00:06:35.170
Next, he aligns the center divot with a
punch and then activates the punch to cut out

00:06:35.170 --> 00:06:37.090
the hole for the lantern lens.

00:06:38.410 --> 00:06:43.120
The craftsman now bends wire to match the
profile of the lantern door.

00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:51.810
He aligns the wire with the scribed lines on
the edge of the door and folds the metal over

00:06:51.810 --> 00:06:56.370
it. Bending the door to the correct
curvature completes the part.

00:06:58.000 --> 00:06:59.560
Following another pattern.

00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:03.970
The craftsman marks the location for vent
holes in the blank that will become the

00:07:03.970 --> 00:07:05.650
Lantern's main structure.

00:07:07.330 --> 00:07:12.010
He cuts out the vent holes where he's made
the marks using a hand-operated punch.

00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:18.000
He then rolls the blank into a cylinder.

00:07:19.450 --> 00:07:23.080
It takes a couple of passes to achieve the
correct curvature.

00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:32.250
Moving on to the lantern's lens holder, the
craftsman crimps a bead around one end.

00:07:32.370 --> 00:07:36.120
This bead helps to retain the bull's eye
lens in the holder.

00:07:38.080 --> 00:07:42.580
Returning to the lantern body, he hammers the
top rim around the cap.

00:07:44.390 --> 00:07:49.220
He preps the surface for soldering with a
chemical cleaning agent known as flux.

00:07:51.010 --> 00:07:54.760
He then solders the joint to secure the top
to the lantern.

00:07:57.520 --> 00:08:00.490
He also solders a raised panel to the back.

00:08:00.580 --> 00:08:03.550
This substantial panel serves as support for
handles.

00:08:08.380 --> 00:08:10.690
He then cleans the solder joints with
acetone.

00:08:14.770 --> 00:08:20.050
Next, he wraps metal hinges around the wire
that runs through the notches in the door.

00:08:20.230 --> 00:08:25.630
He crimps the hinges together at the ends
and positions the door on the lantern body.

00:08:25.750 --> 00:08:29.650
He adjusts the hinges so the ends at level
on the lantern.

00:08:31.510 --> 00:08:33.610
He solders the hinges to the steel
structure.

00:08:39.690 --> 00:08:44.490
The craftsman inserts the bull's eye lens
assembly into the hole in the center of the

00:08:44.490 --> 00:08:51.210
lantern door, and he solders the joint he
pins and solders the two tears of a copper

00:08:51.210 --> 00:08:57.690
chimney. He places the chimney over the hole
in the top of the lantern and tucks more pins

00:08:57.690 --> 00:08:59.370
into holes in the chimney.

00:09:00.150 --> 00:09:05.130
The craftsman installs a decorative part in
the top one that won't obstruct the chimney

00:09:05.130 --> 00:09:10.230
hole. He assembles the handles to the raised
panel at the back of the lantern.

00:09:13.190 --> 00:09:20.630
Once the soldered seam hardens, he files it
down, the craftsman test the latch on the

00:09:20.630 --> 00:09:22.670
door and confirms that it operates
perfectly.

00:09:26.570 --> 00:09:31.250
After taping up the lens and handles, he
spray paints the lantern black.

